{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"ALSA-2026:95370","published":"2026-11-05T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-11-05T19:45:02.312167367Z","related":["CVE-2026-64541","CVE-2026-68162","CVE-2026-68451","CVE-2026-68452","CVE-2026-72080","CVE-2026-72221","CVE-2026-72222","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-74588","CVE-2026-74752","CVE-2026-80553","CVE-2026-80571","CVE-2026-80584","CVE-2026-89479","CVE-2026-89488","CVE-2026-98403"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-64541","CVE-2026-68162","CVE-2026-68451","CVE-2026-68452","CVE-2026-72080","CVE-2026-72221","CVE-2026-72222","CVE-2026-74586","CVE-2026-74588","CVE-2026-74752","CVE-2026-80553","CVE-2026-80571","CVE-2026-80584","CVE-2026-89479","CVE-2026-89488","CVE-2026-98403"],"summary":"Important: kernel security update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: net/smc: fix UAF in smc_cdc_rx_handler() by pinning the socket (CVE-2026-64541)\n  * kernel: sctp: avoid auth_enable sysctl UAF during netns teardown (CVE-2026-68162)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA AES cipher key requests (CVE-2026-68452)\n  * kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA ECC private key requests (CVE-2026-68451)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)\n  * kernel: fs/resctrl: Fix use-after-free during unmount (CVE-2026-72080)\n  * kernel: sctp: keep chunk->transport in step with the list it is queued on (CVE-2026-74588)\n  * kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)\n  * kernel: sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use (CVE-2026-74752)\n  * kernel: s390/vfio_ccw: Cancel existing workqueues (CVE-2026-80553)\n  * kernel: powerpc/pseries: papr-phy-attest - validate cmd.length, plug mem leak (CVE-2026-80571)\n  * kernel: s390/qeth: validate user buffer length in SNMP and ARP query 